Z||000003||goldiron||09-19-2001||11:27 PM||||Is relay deemed ok because you jumpered the passenger side motor leads (at the relay connector) to the driver side motor terminals on the relay and it works?<BR>The '87 wiring diagram shows only a dark green lead and a grey lead running from the motor to the relay (terminals c and d).  No brown wire shown. Might check both fusible links in the two red wires in the front light harness.  They are located on right side of master cylinder. Can't tell from schematic how they influence left vs right operation.  good luck.||||reg||1
