Z||000006||theogre||09-22-2001||01:32 PM||||There is no brown wire in that system... <P>The motor runs down properly.... I'm guessing you swapped the 2 relays side to side and still hade the same result. That would seem to point to the third relay or the switch in the motor.<P>It sounds like the thing is wired ok but without actually seeing it its hard to tell. There are several variations of green wires under the hood. It's hard to say exactly what it could be.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Matthew_Fiero||09-23-2001||08:44 AM||||That brown wire i speak of, it is connected )with electrical tape) to a smaller green wire, it runs with all the wires that lead to the radiator but it stops near the headlights, i wonder what it could be...<BR>it can't be anything in the motor, because i swapped motors for a second and it goes up and down. and i have swapped relays with the other relay as well.||||reg||1
